cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Safe-ICE: Safe Cross-Entropy-Based Importance Sampling for rare event simulation"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  paper describing the underlying method.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Diogo
    family-names: Ribeiro
    email: dfr@esmad.ipp.pt
    affiliation: ESMAD, Instituto Politécnico do Porto
repository-code: "https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/adaptive-importance-sampling-ice"
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of the Safe Cross-Entropy-Based Importance Sampling
  (Safe-ICE) algorithm for estimating small failure probabilities in
  reliability analysis, including the von Mises-Fisher-Nakagami mixture model,
  a penalized EM optimizer for automatic component selection, and heavy-tailed
  exploration via the inverse Nakagami distribution.
keywords:
  - importance sampling
  - rare event simulation
  - reliability analysis
  - Monte Carlo
  - cross-entropy method
  - structural reliability
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
